      "Key": "seduce",
      "Title": "Seduce, don\u0027t just observe",
      "Status": "fail",
      "Evidence": "The prose is meticulous and controlled \u2014 the hum, the worn handholds outside 5-C, the commons wall\u0027s repainted numbers \u2014 but these textures are deployed as thematic reinforcement of the ledger-and-loss structure rather than as seductive, strange-beautiful sensory hooks; the piece opens with dry procedural exposition (stress readings, coherence decay curves, wrist displays) and stays in that register throughout, so allure never precedes or exceeds the accurate observation.",
      "Fix": "Open with a sustained, sensory immersion in Candelaria\u0027s specific wrongness-made-beautiful (the sound of a bloc breathing, the smell of sixty-year-old recycled air, the vertiginous view through the outer ring) before pivoting to Teo\u0027s clinical readings, so the reader falls in love with the place before the ledger starts subtracting from it."
    },
    {
      "Key": "open_grounded",
      "Title": "Open with the world doing its work",
      "Status": "pass",
      "Evidence": "The opening beats \u2014 Teo checking stress readings on the gantry, the commons wall ritual of repainting the altitude number, the walk deck-by-deck through worn handholds and the machine shop sign \u2014 establish the world\u0027s ordinary texture (the Hush, freeboard, Air Tax) entirely through a character who has stopped being surprised by any of it, before the AshgraveMaterials letter introduces plot pressure.",
      "Fix": null
    },
    {
      "Key": "gloss_in_voice",
      "Title": "Gloss first mentions in-voice, never dump",
      "Status": "pass",
      "Evidence": "Terms like \u0027the Hush\u0027 (coherence drivers holding the bloc aloft), \u0027The Low\u0027 (no governance line, no Air Tax bracket, salvage waiting for a claimant), \u0027Air Tax\u0027 (a fee on altitude explained in one clause), and \u0027freeboard\u0027 (glossed via the surface-hull analogy \u0027back when hulls floated on water\u0027) are each folded into Teo\u0027s working thoughts as she\u0027d actually think them, oriented at first use without stopping the narrative to explain.",
      "Fix": null
    },
    {
      "Key": "acronym_after_term",
      "Title": "Never an acronym before its term",
      "Status": "warn",
      "Evidence": "The story is scrupulous about most in-universe jargon (e.g. \u0027Air Tax,\u0027 \u0027freeboard,\u0027 \u0027certified salvage\u0027 are all glossed), but the currency symbol \u0027\u03A6\u0027 is used from its very first appearance (\u0027Total offer: \u03A6847,000\u0027) with no explanation of what it stands for or how to read it, and \u0027NSB\u0027-style acronyms are otherwise avoided entirely, suggesting the rule was followed for true acronyms but the symbol itself was never glossed.",
      "Fix": "Add a brief in-voice gloss the first time \u03A6 appears, e.g. having Teo mentally note \u0027\u03A6 \u2014 Phos, the city\u0027s standard currency mark\u0027 before or as she reads the AshgraveMaterials letter."
    },
    {
      "Key": "human_crack",
      "Title": "Give the POV character one human crack",
      "Status": "warn",
      "Evidence": "The clearest human crack for Teo is the tether-platform photograph \u0027propped against the wall where it always sat, never hung \u2014 because hanging it would have meant deciding it belonged somewhere permanent, and she still wasn\u0027t sure it did,\u0027 paired with her fifty-one-kilo life and the realization that her own lightness kept her from understanding what weight costs others until Prita\u0027s hand pressed to her sternum.",
      "Fix": "Let that photograph beat breathe a moment longer with a concrete sensory or memory detail (what\u0027s in the photo, who\u0027s in it) rather than only abstracting it into the \u0027permanence\u0027 theme, so the crack lands as a felt image instead of another analytical observation."
    },
